WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Once there was a child. His parents got up in the morning and told him to hurry out.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Before setting out, he drank a cup of strong tea. That tea…

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.800
He said, “Mom, this tea is bitter.” She said, “Stir it, and it won’t be bitter.”

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
He stirred it for ages, but it was still bitter. He stirred hard and kept stirring, but it was still bitter.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
His mother said, “Oh, sorry. I forgot to add sugar. I forgot the sugar; no amount of stirring will change it.”

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Today, we keep stirring through life: earning money, studying, looking for a spouse, having children, striving and working hard.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Right? After all that stirring, we still have to sing “A Cup Full of Bitter Wine.”

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
We sing “Tomorrow Will Be Better,” then “If You Strive, You Will Win,” and later, “Nothing to Fear.”

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Then we compare ourselves and put on a show. We become obsessed with saving face, and end up unhappy.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Life passes by in this uncertainty. Dear friends, we have all been through this.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.000
But today, we are glad to tell you: who is this God?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:28.000
He is the One who is, who was, and who is to come—the Almighty.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
He is not a god carved from wood, nor a god from the stories in Investiture of the Gods.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.000
He is the God who created heaven and earth, with a will, a purpose, a plan, and an eternal purpose.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.000
With this God as your support, you can be at peace.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:52.000
He was promised in the Old Testament, which also foretold that He would come among humanity

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
to resolve humanity’s predicament. He would be called Immanuel, meaning “God with us.”

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.000
That name is Jesus. Who is Jesus?

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:14.000
Jesus is not merely a figure in history. He is the One foretold again and again across four thousand years of the Old Testament.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:26.000
He is God becoming man. “Ye” in Jesus points to Jehovah God in the Old Testament; “su” speaks of Jehovah God coming to be our salvation

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.880
and our Savior. Dear friends…
